        "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx=$",
        "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{3x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(3x-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1)^{4}}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
